00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:05.430 align:start position:0%
there is a cold silence before easter  sunday service at this catholic church  in kiev  worshipers kneel and cross themselves as  they come in  some take confession while the  congregation gathers  many of the people here have family  members and friends fighting in the east  most never expected they would have to  live through war  prejudice  everyone is living through their own  personal pain and they know some of the  people they know may not come home  and by coming here we look for belief  and hope because maybe there will be  nothing left  there are more than a million roman  catholics in this predominantly orthodox  christian country  boxes of donated food and clothing are  stacked along the isles ready for  volunteers among the worshippers to  distribute to those in need  father pavlov viskovsky prepares to give  communion the congregation  wait in line  when the war started i started coming to  the church more often because of the  anxiety when i hear the father's  preaching it gets easier i find more  faith in myself in our society and our  victory  in a corner of the church stands a model  of an army post with the ukrainian flag  recently services have had to be held on  the ground near the church crypt  until a few days ago church services in  recent weeks have been held here  underground because of fear of potential  russian shelling  now despite the fact that russian forces  have withdrawn from areas around kiev  there is still great fear that that  shelling could start again the head  priest here  says that he estimates up to 80 percent  of the worshipers in this parish have  fled since the war began  the priests resisted government pressure  to close the church on february the 24th  when the russian army invaded  the day the war started officials told  us we had to close the church but we  refused because we had to support the  people we have since helped evacuate  children and the elderly from areas of  the parish outside cave the atmosphere  in the church has changed  since the war started people are more  united and we help each other more  a priest collects money to go towards  renovations of the church damaged by  fire last year  because without this place of worship  many of the people here would find  living through war even harder than it  already is  chance stratfor al jazeera kiev
 

